      "copy": "Captain Blood turns a science-fiction journey into an encounter with other forms of intelligence. Released in 1988, it is remembered for an unusual proposition: travelling through an alien universe means trying to communicate with its inhabitants. Understanding becomes part of exploration, rather than simply a reward for reaching the next location.\n\nARTE’s retrospective places it among the distinctive experiments of French game production. Its presence beside Méwilo is deliberate. These games do not look alike, tell the same stories, or imagine the same player. Their connection is a willingness to question what an adventure can be about.\n\nHere, the screen becomes a meeting place with something initially difficult to read. The player must attend, interpret, and build a relationship with an unfamiliar world. This exhibition reads that emphasis on communication as an early counterpart to later games that make language, perspective, or understanding their central action.",
