      "deck": "A small figure inside a world with a large imagination.",
      "copy": "Released in 1994, Little Big Adventure follows Twinsen through a world threatened by Dr FunFrock. Adeline Software combines a distinctive viewpoint, physical movement, conversations, and an adventure that moves between the whimsical and the unsettling. Philippe Vachey’s music is part of its lasting identity.\n\nThe game offers another path through the decade’s experiments in three dimensions. Rather than making realism the only destination, it builds a coherent world through scale, staging, and character. Its original manual credits Adeline’s game design to an idea by Frédérick Raynal, whose earlier Alone in the Dark explored a very different atmosphere.\n\nLittle Big Adventure 2 follows in 1997. Together, the games remind us that technical change does not produce one inevitable style. New tools can support menace, comedy, wonder, or political fable. The important historical question is not only how many dimensions a game displays, but what its creators choose to do with them.",
