      "copy": "Cryo’s Atlantis: The Lost Tales, released in 1997, places the player in the role of Seth, a new member of Queen Rhea’s guard. Its first-person adventure unfolds through exploration, conversation, and puzzles in a richly imagined lost civilisation.\n\nThe game exemplifies a different use of the CD-ROM’s audiovisual possibilities from a fast-moving action game. Environments, voices, and music establish a world that asks to be examined. The pace creates room for attention: a building, an object, or a conversation can become the next piece of a larger mystery.\n\nPlaced beside Dune and Versailles, Atlantis shows the breadth of Cryo’s interests, from literary science fiction to historical reconstruction and myth. This is not a single formula for French adventure. It is a record of a studio using the same developing medium to propose very different places for a player to inhabit.",
