      "copy": "Syberia, released in 2002, follows Kate Walker through a world shaped by Benoît Sokal’s visual imagination. Its adventure connects an unfolding journey with intricate environments, mechanical inventions, and characters whose lives extend beyond the immediate puzzle.\n\nMicroids’s retrospective describes the importance of a coherent relationship between the world, the story, and sound. The setting is not simply a container for the narrative: its details carry the feeling of the journey. Sokal’s background as a comics artist also makes Syberia an important meeting point between drawn storytelling and the interactive image.\n\nAt a time when larger real-time worlds are becoming a dominant ambition, the game sustains another tradition: the authored adventure, organised around looking, listening, and understanding. A French production history includes these competing tempos. Technical progress does not make the quieter pleasure of a carefully composed scene disappear.",
