      "copy": "Ubisoft Montpellier’s Beyond Good & Evil is released in 2003. Its protagonist, Jade, is an investigative reporter drawn into a conflict in which appearances and official explanations cannot be taken for granted. Alongside companions including Pey’j, she explores a world where discovering evidence matters.\n\nThe game combines movement, action, and an investigative premise rather than placing the player in a single narrow role. This mixture gives its world a distinctive rhythm: a journey through places is also a process of reconsidering what those places mean.\n\nIts inclusion complicates an easy division between a major publisher and an independent auteur tradition. Large organisations can also be the sites of particular, recognisable creative experiments. The French history of games is not a simple transfer of imagination from small teams to big studios; it is an ongoing negotiation between teams, resources, production structures, and a work’s individual character.",
