      "copy": "Trackmania’s first release arrives on 21 November 2003. Nadeo’s racing game places the construction of tracks alongside the act of driving them. The course is not only something supplied by the developer: it can become a player’s own design, shared with other people.\n\nThe official twentieth-anniversary retrospective stresses this history of community creation. A distinctive approach to racing without car-to-car collisions puts attention on the route and the attempt. Competition becomes a relationship with a time, a line, and a sequence that can be tried again.\n\nThis changes the scale of authorship. One team makes the tools and the rules, while players continually make new places in which those rules can operate. A history focused only on a game’s first release would miss much of what makes it culturally significant. Trackmania asks us to include the people who keep building after the box has left the shop.",
