      "copy": "Launched in 2004, DOFUS places Ankama’s World of Twelve at the centre of an online role-playing experience. The Roubaix company’s history connects games with animation, comics, and other forms of storytelling, allowing the same imagined universe to be encountered in different media.\n\nAn online world has a different historical rhythm from a single-player adventure. Its meaning develops through repeated visits, shared experiences, and the continuing relationship between a production team and its players. The launch date identifies a beginning, rather than a finished cultural object.\n\nAnkama also makes the map of French development more precise. Paris is not the only centre of production: Roubaix belongs beside Lyon, Montpellier, Bordeaux, and other local scenes. In this exhibition, DOFUS represents a form of collective world-building in which the studio’s visual language and the community’s life become inseparable parts of the work’s history.",
