      "copy": "Released on 5 July 2016, Furi combines close-range sword fighting with twin-stick shooting in a sequence of demanding encounters. The Game Bakers organise the experience around a small set of actions: attack, dodge, parry, and learn what an opponent is about to do.\n\nIts intensity is carefully composed. Character designs by Takashi Okazaki meet an electronic soundtrack with contributors including Carpenter Brut, Danger, and The Toxic Avenger. The work draws its energy from collaboration across disciplines and borders, rather than from a supposedly pure national style.\n\nIn this museum, Furi offers a counterpoint to the expansive worlds of the previous room. A game can feel ambitious through concentration. A limited arena, a repeated gesture, and a change in musical pressure can be enough to make an encounter memorable. Independent production includes both the pleasure of exploration and the precision of a single, demanding moment.",
