      "copy": "Sloclap releases Sifu on 8 February 2022. The Paris studio builds its action game around close combat, observation, and repeated practice. Its martial-arts focus asks the player to read movement and respond with intention, rather than treating every encounter as an interchangeable obstacle.\n\nThe work is useful to a history of French production precisely because its cultural references do not stop at France’s borders. Where a game is made and what it draws upon are different questions. The history becomes richer when both are kept in view.\n\nPlaced near Dead Cells and Furi, Sifu also suggests a connection between repetition and expression. Trying again is not simply a delay before the story resumes. It can be the central experience: a process through which the player’s understanding changes. This is a curatorial connection between distinct games, not a claim that their systems or their production histories are identical.",
