      "copy": "Developed by Toulouse’s Rundisc and released in 2023, Chants of Sennaar builds its adventure around deciphering unfamiliar languages. Its tower, inspired by the story of Babel, brings the player into contact with groups whose words and ways of life must gradually be understood.\n\nObservation and interpretation become the means of progress. A symbol gains meaning through its use, a place provides context, and a tentative reading can change as the player learns more. The game makes an intellectual activity feel spatial and tangible.\n\nBeside Captain Blood, it invites a long view of French adventure games that place communication at the centre of play. The connection is interpretive, not a claim of direct influence. More than three decades separate these works, yet both allow the encounter with another world to begin with a question: how can I understand someone whose language I do not yet share?",
